Vita: --vita-fast-gen-mode=off|on|verify (platform/vita/runtime/fast_painter.hpp). BP genMode (0x00)
and XF numChans (0x09) / numTexGens (0x3F) set the same state fields, so each handler invalidates
the other shadow register. J3D sends all three with every material: a material sent again was
handled again every time, the pipeline was marked changed, and the draw rebuilt its config, looked
it up and rebuilt the uniforms to find the pipeline it already had.
On: a write that leaves the decoded state as it is only makes its shadow register valid again. It
sets no dirty flag and invalidates nothing. That is a genMode write of the value its shadow holds
when every field it decodes equals the state, and a numChans / numTexGens write of the state value.
A valid shadow always decodes to the state fields (only these three handlers write them), so the
writes skipped afterwards as unchanged would have written the values the state holds.
Verify: such a write is handled as before, with its pipeline flag kept apart (DirtyRevalidated).
The draw rebuilds the pipeline as before and counts the rebuilds only such writes asked for, and
those that gave a different pipeline. Off (the default): one test per handled write of the three.

